"Models | ChatGPT Learn (https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/models?surface=web)\nciteturn14view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/models?surface=web\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1138\nL0: For the complete documentation index, see 【0†llms.txt】. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending `.md` to the page URL.\nL1: \nL2: 【1†ChatGPT】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†Home】\nL5: \nL6: 【2†API】\nL7: \nL8: 【3†ChatGPT】\nL9: \nL10: 【4†Docs】\nL11: \nL12: 【5†Use cases】\nL13: \nL14: 【6†Training】\nL15: \nL16: 【7†Resources】\nL17: \nL18: 【8†Resources】\nL19: \nL20: 【4†Overview】 【9†Features】 【10†Configuration】 【11†Developers】 【12†Security】 【13†Administration】 【5†Use Cases】 【7†Resources】\nL21: \nL22: ## Search the docs\nL23: \nL24: Search docs[Input: Start searching]\nL25: ### Suggested\nL26: \nL27: [Button: responses create][Button: reasoning_effort][Button: realtime][Button: prompt caching]\nL28: \nL29: Primary navigation\nL30: \nL31: [Button: API ][Button: ChatGPT ][Button: Docs ][Button: Use cases ][Button: Training ][Button: Resources ][Button: Resources ]\nL32: \nL33: Search docs[Input: Start searching]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nImageOps module - Pillow (PIL Fork) 13.0.0 documentation (https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/ImageOps.html)\nciteturn14view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn13view1\",\"pattern\":\"EXIF Orientation\"}); Total lines: 510\nL374: PIL.ImageOps.exif_transpose(image: 【137†Image】, * (Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)), in_place: Literal[True]) → 【141†None†docs.python.org】【176†[source]】【177†¶】\nL375: PIL.ImageOps.exif_transpose(image: 【137†Image】, * (Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)), in_place: Literal[False] = False) → 【137†Image】\nL376: \nL377: \nL378: If an image has an EXIF Orientation tag, other than 1, transpose the image accordingly, and remove the orientation data.\nL379: \nL380: Parameters:\nL381: \nL382: \nL383:   * image – The image to transpose.\nL384:   * in_place – Boolean. Keyword-only argument. If `True`, the original image is modified in-place, and `None` is returned. If `False` (default), a new 【137†`Image`】 object is returned with the transposition applied. If there is no transposition, a copy of the image will be returned.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nImage file formats - Pillow (PIL Fork) 13.0.0 documentation (https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/handbook/image-file-formats.html)\nciteturn14view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn13view2\",\"pattern\":\"WebP\"}); Total lines: 1720\nL1164: A string containing the desired compression method for the file. (valid only with libtiff installed) Valid compression methods are: 【226†`None`†docs.python.org】, `\"group3\"`, `\"group4\"`, `\"jpeg\"`, `\"lzma\"`, `\"packbits\"`, `\"tiff_adobe_deflate\"`, `\"tiff_ccitt\"`, `\"tiff_lzw\"`, `\"tiff_raw_16\"`, `\"tiff_sgilog\"`, `\"tiff_sgilog24\"`, `\"tiff_thunderscan\"`, `\"webp\"`, `\"zstd\"`\nL1165: \nL1166: quality\nL1167: \nL1168: \nL1169: The image quality for JPEG compression, on a scale from 0 (worst) to 100 (best). The default is 75.\nL1170: \nL1171: Added in version 6.1.0.\nL1172: These arguments to set the tiff header fields are an alternative to using the general tags available through tiffinfo.\nL1173: \nL1174: description\nL1175: \nL1176: software\nL1177: \nL1178: date_time\nL1179: \nL1180: artist\nL1181: \nL1182: copyright\nL1183: \nL1184: \nL1185: Strings\nL1186: \nL1187: icc_profile\nL1188: \nL1189: \nL1190: The ICC Profile to include in the saved file.\nL1191: \nL1192: resolution_unit\nL1193: \nL1194: \nL1195: An integer. 1 for no unit, 2 for inches and 3 for centimeters.\nL1196: \nL1197: resolution\nL1198: \nL1199: \nL1200: Either an integer or a float, used for both the x and y resolution.\nL1201: \nL1202: x_resolution\nL1203: \nL1204: \nL1205: Either an integer or a float.\nL1206: \nL1207: y_resolution\nL1208: Either an integer or a float.\nL1209: \nL1210: dpi\nL1211: \nL1212: \nL1213: A tuple of `(x_resolution, y_resolution)`, with inches as the resolution unit. For consistency with other image formats, the x and y resolutions of the dpi will be rounded to the nearest integer.\nL1214: ### WebP【227†¶】\nL1215: \nL1216: Pillow reads and writes WebP files. Requires libwebp v0.5.0 or later.\nL1217: #### Opening【228†¶】\nL1218: \nL1219: The 【136†`open()`】 method sets the following 【143†`info`】 properties:\nL1220: \nL1221: background\nL1222: \nL1223: \nL1224: Background color of the canvas, as an RGBA tuple with values in the range of (0-255).\nL1225: \nL1226: loop\nL1227: \nL1228: \nL1229: The number of times the WEBP should loop. 0 means that it will loop forever.\nL1230: \nL1231: icc_profile\nL1232: \nL1233: \nL1234: May not be present. The ICC color profile for the image.\nL1235: \nL1236: exif\nL1237: \nL1238: \nL1239: May not be present. Raw EXIF data from the image.\nL1240: \nL1241: xmp\nL1242: \nL1243: \nL1244: May not be present. Raw XMP data from the image.\nL1245: \nL1246: duration\nL1247: Only present after the current frame is loaded. The time to display the current frame of the WEBP, in milliseconds.\nL1248: \nL1249: timestamp\nL1250: \nL1251: \nL1252: Only present after the current frame is loaded. The total duration of all previous frames of the WEBP, in milliseconds.\nL1253: #### Saving【229†¶】\nL1254: \nL1255: The 【137†`save()`】 method supports the following options:\nL1256: \nL1257: lossless\nL1258: \nL1259: \nL1260: If present and true, instructs the WebP writer to use lossless compression.\nL1261: \nL1262: quality\nL1263: \nL1264: \nL1265: Integer, 0-100, defaults to 80. For lossy, 0 gives the smallest size and 100 the largest. For lossless, this parameter is the amount of effort put into the compression: 0 is the fastest, but gives larger files compared to the slowest, but best, 100.\nL1266: \nL1267: alpha_quality\nL1268: Integer, 0-100, defaults to 100. For lossy compression only. 0 gives the smallest size and 100 is lossless.\nL1269: \nL1270: method\nL1271: \nL1272: \nL1273: Quality/speed trade-off (0=fast, 6=slower-better). Defaults to 4.\nL1274: \nL1275: exact\nL1276: \nL1277: \nL1278: If true, preserve the transparent RGB values. Otherwise, discard invisible RGB values for better compression. Defaults to false.\nL1279: \nL1280: icc_profile\nL1281: \nL1282: \nL1283: The ICC Profile to include in the saved file.\nL1284: \nL1285: exif\nL1286: \nL1287: \nL1288: The exif data to include in the saved file.\nL1289: \nL1290: xmp\nL1291: \nL1292: \nL1293: The XMP data to include in the saved file.\nL1294: #### Saving sequences【230†¶】\nL1295: \nL1296: When calling 【137†`save()`】 to write a WebP file, by default only the first frame of a multiframe image will be saved. If the `save_all` argument is present and true, or if `append_images` is not empty, all frames will be saved, and the following options will also be available.\nL1297: \nL1298: append_images\nL1299: \nL1300: \nL1301: A list of images to append as additional frames. Each of the images in the list can be single or multiframe images.\nL1302: \nL1303: duration\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommand Line Usage | tessdoc (https://tesseract-ocr.github.io/tessdoc/Command-Line-Usage.html)\nciteturn14view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn13view0\",\"pattern\":\"psm\"}); Total lines: 358\nL227:     5       1       1       1       2       3       194     73      139     24      93.263031       $43,456.78\nL228:     5       1       1       1       2       4       350     76      85      25      90.893219       <lazy>\nL229:     5       1       1       1       2       5       451     77      44      19   